# Tenet workspace state (local-only, gitignored by convention)
# UN-ANCHORED 2026-09-16: these were written with a leading `.tenet/`, which git anchors to the
# repo root. A hub started from a SUBDIRECTORY (the init.js:506 cwd-binding bug) writes
# planner/.tenet/ and analytics-mirror/.tenet/ -- none of which these patterns matched, so 2.9 MB
# of stray runtime state sat untracked-but-unignored for two months. `**/` covers both.
**/.tenet/memory.db*
**/.tenet/context-hub.pid
**/.tenet/context-hub.port
**/.tenet/context-hub.token
**/.tenet/logs/
**/.tenet/sessions/
**/.tenet/presence/
**/.tenet/telemetry/
**/.tenet/map-events.jsonl
**/.tenet/service-events.jsonl
**/.tenet/training-buffer.jsonl
**/.tenet/telemetry-agent-state.json

# The workspace journal is the project's decision history -- and this repo is PUBLIC. It is
# backed up ENCRYPTED to the `journals` orphan branch by scripts/backup-journal.sh, never
# committed in the clear: it carries room names, family first names, DHW draw timestamps (an
# occupancy signal) and the property UUID. Scanned clean of credential patterns, encrypted anyway.
**/.tenet/journal/
**/.tenet/build-journal.jsonl
**/.tenet/replay-buffer.jsonl

# Worktrees + temp dirs
worktrees/
.tenet/tmp/

# Node / Python deps
node_modules/
node_modules
.venv/
__pycache__/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Tenet build-agent runner scratch (worktree-local)
EXPERIMENTS.md
AGENT.md
.tenet/provenance-key
